{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1613-ornstein-uhlenbeck-process-horse-race-betting-herding.md", "equation": "Sequential voting model: voter t chooses horse with final share q via X(t,q) ∈ {0,1}; running share Z(n,q) = (1/nΔt)Σ_{s≤nΔt} X(s,q). Micro decision rule f_n(z) = r_inf(n)·q + (1 − r_inf(n))·z — convex mix of informed (f_inf = q) and herder (f_herd = z) rules; herders are Max–Min players (expected return independent of z since odds ∝ 1/z). Gardiner SDE derivation from conditional mean/variance of ΔZ gives the time-inhomogeneous O–U process (Eq. 2), mean-reverting toward q whenever r_inf(n) > 0, in quadratic potential U_n(z) = r_inf(n)/[2(n+1)]·(z−q)². Micro estimation: regress (n+1)(Z(r,h,n+1) − Z(r,h,n)) = −r_inf (Z(r,h,n) − q(r,h)) at n ∈ {1,…,50} (Eq. 11). Macro: compare empirical log MSE(n)/MSE(1) against theory.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9135}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1613-ornstein-uhlenbeck-process-horse-race-betting-herding.md", "equation": "Z(t,q) = (1/t)Σ_{s=1}^{t} X(s,q); ℙ(X=1|Z=z) = f_n(z) = r_inf(n)·q + (1−r_inf(n))·z (Eq. 1).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9135}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1613-ornstein-uhlenbeck-process-horse-race-betting-herding.md", "equation": "dZ(n,q) = −[r_inf(n)(Z(n,q) − q)/(n+1)] dn + [√(q(1−q))/((n+1)√Δt)] dW(n,q) (Eq. 2) — time-inhomogeneous O–U.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9135}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1613-ornstein-uhlenbeck-process-horse-race-betting-herding.md", "equation": "U_n(z) = r_inf(n)/[2(n+1)] (z−q)².", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9135}
