{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1647-deep-evidential-regression.md", "equation": "Place a Normal-Inverse-Gamma prior over the Gaussian likelihood: y ~ N(μ, σ²), μ ~ N(γ, σ²/ν), σ² ~ IG(α, β). The network outputs m = (γ, ν, α, β). Prediction = E[μ] = γ; aleatoric = E[σ²] = β/(α−1); epistemic = Var[μ] = β/(ν(α−1)). Training = multi-task: (1) maximize model evidence → closed-form NLL of the Student-t marginal p(y | m) = St(y; γ, β(1+ν)/(να), 2α); (2) evidence regularizer L^R = | ·(2ν + α) that strips evidence (inflates uncertainty) proportional to error. Total: L = L^NLL + λ·L^R.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9135}
